 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Current unresolved teaching gap
+
+The default sampler draws isolated monochrome 2×2 components, while `self_check`
+accepts unions of overlapping monochrome 2×2 windows. An exact-component rival
+therefore fits the demonstrations but disagrees with the canonical scanning rule
+on a solid 2×3 rectangle. This is the same defect in both current audits, not a
+second finding.
+
+An independent bounded probe of source SHA-256
+`28e54759969936d8e3fe80814cb227f744de2055581b85238a47c2063747403d`
+confirmed the rival fits all four labeled canonical pairs and four fresh medium
+draws (seeds 0–1, sample indices 0–1). Protected Racket returned four colored
+cells on a validator-clean 2×3 color-4 rectangle; the rival returned a blank grid.
+Runnable source, exact inputs/outputs, rule and runtime hashes are in
+`checks/8fbc7756d37f/probe.py` and
+`checks/8fbc7756d37f/probe-result.json` in the review workspace.
+
+Next repair: teach overlapping windows by sampling both isolated 2×2 blocks and
+monochrome 2×3/3×2 rectangles, explicitly revise the isolated-object invariant to
+the window-union contract, and retain a focused canonical-Racket regression for
+both rectangle orientations. The minimum-two-windows validator and existing
+`blocks_overlap` negative texture must be reconciled with that contract. This
+bounded replay leaves the selected generator and canonical rule unchanged; the
+audits remain unresolved. Inherited missing-`RULE_HASH` and singleton-axis lint
+findings were not rerun or cleared.
